Package: homelab-roundcube-account-menu
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, homelab-roundcube (>= 0.1.17)
Description: Gmail-style account menu for an already-installed homelab-roundcube
 A pure PHP/JS Roundcube plugin (homelab_account_menu), shipped as its
 own package rather than bundled into homelab-roundcube itself -- it is
 nothing without Roundcube already installed and configured (hence the
 hard Depends, not a Recommends), so it is an add-on in the true sense:
 postinst verifies homelab-roundcube's own config.inc.php.bootstrapped
 marker exists before touching anything, refusing gracefully (not
 failing the whole apt transaction) if Roundcube is not set up yet.
 .
 Adds a persistent account menu to the top of the webmail UI -- a
 circular avatar showing the signed-in user's initial that opens a
 Gmail-style dropdown: the user's display name and email, a "Manage
 your account" link to the self-service account app
 (myaccount.<domain>, the homelab-accountmanage service), a couple of
 deep links (security, sessions), and "Sign out". It matches the
 top-right profile dropdown the other homelab web apps already show, so
 webmail feels like part of the same suite.
 .
 Holds NO credential and NO database role of its own. "Manage your
 account" is a plain link that auto-logs-in through the shared SSO
 session (the accountmanage app is a registered SSO client); "Sign out"
 reuses Roundcube's own logout command, which already chains through
 homelab-sso's single-logout. The plugin reads only the signed-in
 user's identity from Roundcube's own session -- same minimal trust
 boundary as it takes to render any other skin element.
 .
 Because Roundcube writes config.inc.php exactly once (a .bootstrapped
 marker, never rewritten by dpkg-reconfigure), this package's postinst
 makes a structurally-anchored, idempotent edit to the already-written
 $config['plugins'] array to register itself -- the same technique
 (and the same safety net: backs the file up first, validates with
 php -l, restores on failure) proven by homelab-roundcube-invite.
